<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Ben Simmons on $3.52m in 2026-27?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Simmons is paid <strong>$3.52m</strong> because a maximum contract ended and what replaced it is a minimum deal with none of it guaranteed at signing.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went first overall in 2016 and his rookie contract was worth <strong>$26.62m</strong>.</li>
<li>Philadelphia extended him in 2020 for <strong>$177.24m</strong> across five years.</li>
<li>That deal’s 15% trade bonus was voided when he was traded to <a href="/teams/brooklyn-nets/">Brooklyn</a>.</li>
<li>He earned <strong>$37.89m</strong> in 2023-24 and <strong>$1.08m</strong> the season after.</li>
<li>He tore his Achilles on October 18, 2026, so the full salary is now owed.</li>
</ul>
<p>He is a first overall pick on the veteran minimum at 30.</p>

